0..72 Comment "// The null niche as a realizability predicate. A type\'s realisers are a"
73..153 Comment "// predicate on a word and a heap, `V⟦T⟧ : (Nat, Heap) => Type`; the heap is"
154..223 Comment "// data, the separating conjunction a sigma over a disjoint split and"
224..300 Comment "// points-to a singleton, so the normaliser computes every assertion and the"
301..369 Comment "// kernel replays every declaration here (Wagner, Eisbach and Ahmed,"
370..446 Comment "// \"Realistic Realizability: Specifying ABIs You Can Count On\", OOPSLA 2024,"
447..515 Comment "// doi:10.1145/3689755, § 4.2). `Option<&T>` is one word, null or a"
516..588 Comment "// reference; its realisers are equivalent at every heap to those of the"
589..662 Comment "// two-word tagged layout, and the marshallers between the two meet their"
663..739 Comment "// triples. A C function specified by hand, `deref_or`, is met by the niche;"
740..782 Comment "// its `_Nonnull` neighbour is refused, in"
783..847 Comment "// `../../pathological/specification/niche-realizability.gandr`."
848..850 Comment "//"
851..924 Comment "// Words are `Nat`, null `Zero`, so a case on a word reduces; a triple is"
925..994 Comment "// `P(h) => wp(c, Q, h)`, and a pure marshaller\'s precondition is its"
995..1072 Comment "// postcondition at its answer. Departing from § 4.2: both layouts are words"
1073..1145 Comment "// by value rather than objects behind a reference count, so there is no"
1146..1223 Comment "// `size` and no count; there is no later modality; and a triple is stated at"
1224..1297 Comment "// the heap it owns, with no frame rule over it. Where a realiser runs to"
1298..1346 Comment "// `emp(h)` the proofs case on the heap (#2832)."
1348..1357 Comment "// `Nat`."
